caps: try strict equality before the double subset pass in gst_caps_is_equal

For non-fixed caps, gst_caps_is_equal() runs gst_caps_is_subset() in
both directions. Each subset pass pairwise-intersects structures, which
walks every entry of list-typed fields with full GValue dispatch and
allocation churn.

Callers frequently compare caps with identical contents (sticky caps
deduplication, renegotiation checks). Strict equality catches that case
with a single linear field-by-field compare and fails fast on any
mismatch, so the worst-case overhead for genuinely different caps is
small compared to the retained subset passes.

gstcapsops benchmark (videoconvert-style template with an 82-entry
format list, identical copies): is_equal 19.2 us -> 12.0 us. The
remaining cost is the list compare itself.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/subprojects/gstreamer/gst/gstcaps.c b/subprojects/gstreamer/gst/gstcaps.c
index 7ec84a0929..cb17167d15 100644
--- a/subprojects/gstreamer/gst/gstcaps.c
+++ b/subprojects/gstreamer/gst/gstcaps.c
@@ -1876,6 +1876,13 @@ gst_caps_is_equal (const GstCaps * caps1, const GstCaps * caps2)
   if (G_UNLIKELY (gst_caps_is_fixed (caps1) && gst_caps_is_fixed (caps2)))
     return gst_caps_is_equal_fixed (caps1, caps2);
 
+  /* Callers frequently compare caps with identical contents (e.g. sticky
+   * caps deduplication). Strict equality is a linear field-by-field pass
+   * and much cheaper than the two subset passes below, which pairwise
+   * intersect every structure. It fails fast on a mismatch. */
+  if (gst_caps_is_strictly_equal (caps1, caps2))
+    return TRUE;
+
   return gst_caps_is_subset (caps1, caps2) && gst_caps_is_subset (caps2, caps1);
 }
 

